Rule 1 (type check: input must be Tensor; shape must be list/tuple of ints)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int) ⊎ tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ v_2.len ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (shape (tuple) must provide at least as many sizes as input dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len ≥ ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (shape (list) must provide at least as many sizes as input dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= v_2.len ≥ ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (new leading dimensions (if any) must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int) ⊎ tuple(int)} |= if v_2.len > ndim(v_1) then (∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - ndim(v_1) - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 1)
